  "title": "Decolonization, Inherited Borders and India's Choices",
  "summary": "Decolonization transferred sovereignty to new states while often leaving administrative borders, infrastructure and institutional interfaces created under colonial rule. India's post-independence choices show how a new state can inherit structures while building its own combination of political, economic and civilizational continuity.",
